From 8d8d80692e1985fb89ca2da78758dbb32836ab39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:32:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 34/65] 0033-vela-ue-fsr2-dx11: a DX11 game's FSR 2 on an
 engine FFX backend (AMD UE FSR 2 plugin, RHI backend) runs on OptiScaler's
 DX11 path (Dx11Upscaler / Vela live: sgsr3_12, ffx_12, sgsr2_12)

The UE FSR 2 plugin on D3D11 always uses its RHI backend (FSR2TemporalUpscaler.cpp Initialize: native backends only
for D3D12 / Vulkan): FfxDevice = its FFSR2TemporalUpscaler, callbacks = ffxFsr2GetInterfaceUE, and ffxFsr2ContextDispatch
runs while the render graph is built (FfxCommandList = FRDGBuilder*, FfxResource.resource = FRDGTexture*); the FSR 2
jobs become render-graph compute passes that reach D3D11 later as ID3D11DeviceContext::Dispatch with the jobs' group
counts (FSR2TemporalUpscalerSubPass.h). No native resource exists at the FFX API, so 0029 could not adopt it.

0033: the DX12 FSR 2 create hooks give such a context (DX11 swapchain, FfxDevice no D3D11 / D3D12 device of the game)
a copy of its description with wrapped fpCreatePipeline / fpScheduleGpuJob / fpExecuteGpuJobs (pass id per pipeline,
compute job list per dispatch); its dispatch parameters are kept and the game's FSR 2 still records its passes. A
Detours hook on ID3D11DeviceContext::Dispatch finds the passes by their group counts in job order (reconstruct pass to
last pass), takes colour / depth / MV / exposure from the reconstruct pass SRVs and the reactive mask from the depth
clip pass SRVs (matched to the FFX resource size / format / isDepth, unique only), the output from the last pass UAVs
(output size / format, not an SRV of an FSR 2 pass in this or the last frame = not the ping-pong history), and right
after that pass adopts the context on that context's device (0029 AdoptOnDevice: "context created" line) and runs
Fsr2Dx11Dispatch (NGX DX11 feature, "Vela live: handle N model X" lines), CS shader saved and restored. Not replaced
for 240 frames -> left to the game's FSR 2. VELA_UEFSR2=0 = old behaviour; VELA_UEFSR2_SKIP=1 = once adopted, the
game's own FSR 2 passes from the reconstruct pass on are not dispatched (default: they run, the output is overwritten).
DX12 games: an FfxDevice whose vtable lies in the module of its backend callbacks (UE RHI backend with
r.FidelityFX.FSR2.UseNativeDX12=0) is left to the game instead of getting the latest D3D12 device (crash path).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 4bbae8b996aae67c24140311024e20385b491753)
